WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.040
Hi, I'm Sandra, from HEARa.
Welcome to Day 8 

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.720
of our 10 day Lipreading Challenge, 

3
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.740
designed to help you develop
and practice your lipreading skills. 

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.580
Hearing loss can have a 
profound impact on your life. 

5
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.826
It touches every interaction.

6
00:00:16.826 --> 00:00:18.660
It can affect your career,

7
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:19.980
your relationships,

8
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.300
and your happiness.

9
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:26.520
Join me to explore tips and tricks
on this YouTube channel 

10
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:32.520
to bring confidence and clarity
to relationships in all areas of your life. 

11
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.000
Today we're going to learn
about the TH sound. 

12
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.739
To make this sound,
the tongue is placed between the teeth, 

13
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.013
Watch the word “TEETH" again.
Teeth. 

14
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.699
This sound is relatively easy
to see, especially when 

15
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.140
it's at the beginning of the word. 

16
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.740
Watch this:
THUMB

17
00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.680
For our lipreading practice today,
I'm going to say the sentences 

18
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:02.580
three times. 

19
00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:09.119
First, silently; then, out 
loud; and then, silently again. 

20
00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.439
There's a couple things
I want you to keep in mind 

21
00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.164
for the practice today.

22
00:01:16.164 --> 00:01:21.035
The first thing is that the first time you see the sentence,

23
00:01:21.035 --> 00:01:22.740
try and stay relaxed.

24
00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:27.840
Look for any word or words
that have TH in them, 

25
00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.240
and see if you recognize
any other words. 

26
00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:36.000
Don't try for every single word.
The second thing 

27
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.640
is that you should try
and commit the sentences 

28
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.760
to memory somewhat,
because you'll be seeing them again. 

29
00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:44.422
Are you ready?

30
00:01:44.422 --> 00:01:45.360
Number 1

31
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:56.880
The sentence was:
The third month of the year is March. 

32
